{#
  Intent Buffer Panel - The Frontallappen (Planning Center)

  OPUS-031 Layer 1.5: Shows what the system PLANS to do next.
  OPUS-032 MANAS: Proactive intents from the Cognitive Kernel.

  This is the bridge between Intention and Action:
  - MANAS generates intents proactively (OPUS-032)
  - Human sees them in OPUS.md
  - Human can approve/reject each intent
  - System executes approved intents
  - Result appears in Syscall Console

  THE COGNITIVE LOOP:
  Thinking (MANAS) -> Intention (Buffer) -> Action (Syscall) -> Memory (Console)

  Required context:
    - pending_intent: Dict with:
      For MANAS (source="manas"):
        - intents: List of { id, title, description, priority, risk, reasoning, auto_executable, related_files, related_docs }
        - total_pending: int
        - idle_minutes: int
        - last_thought: str or null
        - recent_executed: List
      For Legacy (source="legacy"):
        - legacy_intent: Dict with old format

  Design Decisions (OPUS-031/032):
    - DD4: Bidirectional Control Surface
    - DD6: Intent before Action (human-in-the-loop)
    - DD7: Proactive Cognition (MANAS generates its own input)
#}

